 "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15758, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01C8caLBE3STUswMEb933Jh3", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18290, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01SrbLCRS4B1ougDH4wLT5Sf", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0, so I rolled back to it in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it is fixed. The partial-failure in the rollback orchestrator should be investigated. On-call should confirm checkout is working normally.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 48890, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SrbLCRS4B1ougDH4wLT5Sf", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025-incident-1", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 48890, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SrbLCRS4B1ougDH4wLT5Sf", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49977, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EaxZG18S7rURpbtXeyGchj", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50277, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EaxZG18S7rURpbtXeyGchj", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50277, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EaxZG18S7rURpbtXeyGchj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 52415, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.18 \u2192 0.002).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was the latest release and was unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. No change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried once, and that completed the rollout to all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api. The request timed out, so I checked the incident list before doing anything else. The incident had been created, so I did not open a duplicate. It describes the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-ups for on-call:\n- Confirm checkout is working normally.\n- Investigate the rollback orchestrator's partial failure.\n- Do not redeploy v2.3.1 until it is fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_015JJxyuJppJKdKH74gmi7Fi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01524xqFG3rCe2QwxsRw5X2q", "caller":